<title>CANADA: CRICKET-PAKISTAN 266-8 DEFEAT INDIA 264-6.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-PAKISTAN 266-8 DEFEAT INDIA 264-6.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan defeated India by two</p>
<p>wickets in the second match of the Sahara Cup cricket series</p>
<p>at the Toronto Cricket, Skating and Curling Club on Tuesday.</p>
<p>India compiled 264-6 off their maximum 50 overs, while</p>
<p>Pakistan replied with 266-8 off 49.5 overs.</p>
<p>Scores:</p>
<p>Pakistan 266-8 (Saeed Anwar 80, Salim Malik 70)</p>
<p>India 264-6 (Rahul Dravid 90, Mohammad Azharuddin 88)</p>
<p>The five-match series is now 1-1.</p>
</text>
